1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,440
The sun goddess Amaterasu withdrew into a

2
00:00:03,440 --> 00:00:06,520
heavenly cave after violent conduct by her

3
00:00:06,520 --> 00:00:09,500
brother Susanoo. With her light hidden,

4
00:00:10,320 --> 00:00:12,080
darkness settled across the world.

5
00:00:12,840 --> 00:00:14,680
The other gods gathered outside.

6
00:00:15,380 --> 00:00:18,820
Fields and living creatures waited without sunlight.

7
00:00:19,340 --> 00:00:21,360
They could not simply command the cave

8
00:00:21,360 --> 00:00:21,920
to open.

9
00:00:22,940 --> 00:00:26,200
The goddess Ame-no-Uzume began a wild dance.

10
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:29,940
The assembled gods laughed so loudly that

11
00:00:29,940 --> 00:00:32,681
curiosity stirred behind the stone door.

12
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:36,980
Amaterasu peered out to discover why everyone

13
00:00:36,980 --> 00:00:38,800
celebrated without her.

14
00:00:39,180 --> 00:00:41,340
A sacred mirror caught her eye,

15
00:00:41,620 --> 00:00:43,770
and the gods seized their chance.

16
00:00:44,940 --> 00:00:46,160
The cave opened fully,

17
00:00:46,160 --> 00:00:48,780
and light poured back over heaven and

18
00:00:48,780 --> 00:00:51,740
earth. A rope marked the passage that

19
00:00:51,740 --> 00:00:53,384
must not close again.

20
00:00:54,484 --> 00:00:55,740
In this myth,

21
00:00:56,240 --> 00:00:58,500
even the sun returns through ingenuity,

22
00:00:59,680 --> 00:01:02,160
ritual, and laughter not force alone.

23
00:01:02,740 --> 00:01:05,080
The world needed every god to work

24
00:01:05,080 --> 00:01:05,480
together.
